<section id="Ch1" class="ltx_chapter">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_chapter"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_chapter">Chapter 1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="Ch1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sequence-to-sequence models have become central in Artificial Intelligence, particularly following the introduction of the transformer architecture. While initially developed for Natural Language Processing, these models have demonstrated utility across domains. A notable example is Computer Vision, where vision transformers are increasingly displacing traditional convolutional neural networks.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Sequence-to-sequence models require mechanisms to exchange information along the time dimension, typically using recurrent or self-attention layers. Recurrent layers need to compress the past into a fixed-size state, while self-attention uses a state that grows linearly with the sequence length. Denoting the sequence length as <math id="Ch1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, the time complexity of recurrent layers is <math id="Ch1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, but this cannot be parallelized easily. Self-attention, on the other hand, is <math id="Ch1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(S^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(S^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> but it is easily parallelizable. The quadratic complexity of self-attention becomes a problem when the sequence length is significantly larger than the feature dimension, which is the case that we focus on. We propose Poolformer, a sequence-to-sequence model that replaces self-attention layers with recurrent layers, and that makes use of pooling to reduce the sequence length. We evaluate our model on raw audio, which naturally features long sequence lengths.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Chapter 2 contains all the theoretical background. It starts by reviewing signal processing concepts, such as <math id="Ch1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-law-encoding (used to quantize audio before feeding it to a model), the fast Fourier transform (used to perform convolutions in linearithmic time), and mel-spectrograms (used to compute the FID and IS metrics). It continues explaining metrics used to assess the quality and diversity of generative models. We then review different kinds of sequence-to-sequence models: recurrent neural networks, self-attention, and state-space models. Finally, we explain how to parallelize recurrent neural networks using convolutions and associative scans.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Chapter 3 presents our proposed Poolformer model, that is defined recursively using SkipBlocks, which contain residual blocks, a down-pooling layer, a nested SkipBlock, an up-pooling layer, and additional residual blocks. We also explain different design decisions such as skip-connection placement, pooling and gating.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Chapter 4 presents our experiments on raw audio data. We conduct extensive experiments to support our architectural choices from Chapter 3. Our results show that pooling greatly accelerates training, improves perceptual metrics (FID and IS), and prevents overfitting. They also suggest that long-range dependencies are handled by deep layers, while shallow layers take care of short-term features. In addition, Poolformer outperforms state-of-the-art models such as SaShiMi <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> and Mamba <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Chapter 5 contains the conclusions, and future research directions, that include applications to text and vision, as well as multi-modal scenarios, where a Poolformer-based LLM could effectively process dense representations of images and videos.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2" class="ltx_chapter">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_chapter"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_chapter">Chapter 2 </span>Theoretical background</h2>

<div id="Ch2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This chapter starts by reviewing signal processing concepts, such as <math id="Ch2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-law-encoding (used to quantize audio before feeding it to a model), the fast Fourier transform (used to perform convolutions in linearithmic time), and mel-spectrograms (used to compute the FID and IS metrics). It continues explaining metrics used to assess the quality and diversity of generative models. We then review different kinds of sequence-to-sequence models: recurrent neural networks, self-attention, and state-space models. Finally, we explain how to parallelize recurrent neural networks using convolutions and associative scans.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch2.S1" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2.1 </span>Signal Processing</h3>

<section id="Ch2.S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1.1 </span>Mu-law encoding</h4>

<div id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Most WAV files contain uncompressed audio with 16 bits per sample. If we feed this raw into a sequence-to-sequence model, we would need a vocabulary size of <math id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{16}=65536" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>16</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>65536</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{16}=65536</annotation></semantics></math>. Even though this is not massive for today’s standards, it makes experiments slower. In addition, most of the related literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> uses a vocabulary size of <math id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{8}</annotation></semantics></math>. For this reason, we use 8-bit samples, and defer 16-bit samples for future work.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To quantize the samples, we use <math id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-law encoding, that expands small amplitudes, and squashes large ones. This makes sense because most natural audio signals have a higher density of information at lower amplitudes, while large amplitudes are less frequent. By applying <math id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-law encoding, we allocate more quantization levels to small amplitudes (where human perception is more sensitive), and fewer levels to large amplitudes.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="Thmdefinition1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-law encoding)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)=\sgn(x)\dfrac{\ln(1+\mu|x|)}{\ln(1+\mu)},\quad-1\leq x\leq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)=\sgn(x)\dfrac{\ln(1+\mu|x|)}{\ln(1+\mu)},\quad-1\leq x\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="Thmdefinition2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-law decoding)<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{-1}(y)=\sgn(y)\dfrac{(1+\mu)^{|y|}-1}{\mu},\quad-1\leq y\leq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{-1}(y)=\sgn(y)\dfrac{(1+\mu)^{|y|}-1}{\mu},\quad-1\leq y\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first map a 16-bit integer to the continuous interval <math id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, then apply <math id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, and finally quantize the result to an 8-bit integer. We can undo this process by using <math id="Ch2.S1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, though there will be some information loss due to quantization. This is visualized in Figure <a href="#Ch2.F1" title="Figure 2.1 ‣ 2.1.1 Mu-law encoding ‣ 2.1 Signal Processing ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch2.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="Ch2.F1.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02206v1/mu-law-fn.svg" id="Ch2.F1.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/358;" width="476" height="358"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F1.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="Ch2.F1.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.F1.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">-law encoding function</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="Ch2.F1.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02206v1/mu-law-example.svg" id="Ch2.F1.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/358;" width="476" height="358"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F1.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="Ch2.F1.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of different quantization schemes</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2.1</span>: </span><math id="Ch2.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">-law encoding visualization<span id="Ch2.F1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. The <math id="Ch2.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-law function (left) compresses large amplitudes and expands small ones. When applied to a signal (right), it produces a “stretched” waveform.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1.2 </span>Fourier transform</h4>

<div id="Ch2.S1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is often useful to transform raw audio waveforms to the frequency domain, as many audio properties are more easily analyzed in this representation. Our goal will be to transform audio signals (one-dimensional sequences) to mel-spectrograms, which have two dimensions: time and frequency.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fourier transform)<span id="Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be Lebesgue integrable, then</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(\omega)=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}f(x)\exp(-2\pi i\omega x)\,dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(\omega)=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}f(x)\exp(-2\pi i\omega x)\,dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Inverse Fourier transform)<span id="Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}\colon\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}\colon\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be Lebesgue integrable, then</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\hat{f}(\omega)\exp(2\pi i\omega x)\,d\omega." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\hat{f}(\omega)\exp(2\pi i\omega x)\,d\omega.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Fourier transform reveals the amplitude and phase of each frequency component present in the signal. While the Fourier transform is a powerful theoretical tool, practical applications, especially in digital signal processing, deal with discrete-time signals and require computationally feasible algorithms. This leads to the discrete Fourier transform (DFT) and its efficient implementation, the fast Fourier transform (FFT).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1.3 </span>Discrete Fourier Transform</h4>

<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Discrete Fourier transform)<span id="Thmdefinition5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\DFT(f)_{k}=\hat{f}_{k}=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}f_{j}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>DFT</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\DFT(f)_{k}=\hat{f}_{k}=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}f_{j}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Discrete inverse Fourier transform)<span id="Thmdefinition6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}\in\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}\in\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\IDFT(\hat{f})_{k}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\hat{f}_{j}\exp\left(ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>IDFT</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\IDFT(\hat{f})_{k}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\hat{f}_{j}\exp\left(ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The inverse discrete Fourier transform can be expressed in terms of the discrete Fourier transform.</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\IDFT\left(\hat{f}\right)=\frac{1}{n}\DFT\left(\hat{f}^{*}\right)^{*}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>IDFT</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>DFT</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\IDFT\left(\hat{f}\right)=\frac{1}{n}\DFT\left(\hat{f}^{*}\right)^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch2.S1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{1}{n}\text{DFT}(\hat{f}^{*})^{*}\right)_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>DFT</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{1}{n}\text{DFT}(\hat{f}^{*})^{*}\right)_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\hat{f}_{j}^{*}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)\right)^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\hat{f}_{j}^{*}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)\right)^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\hat{f}_{j}\exp\left(ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\hat{f}_{j}\exp\left(ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\IDFT\left(\hat{f}\right)_{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>IDFT</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\IDFT\left(\hat{f}\right)_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the discrete Fourier transform is a linear operator, so the operation can be expressed as</p>
<table id="Ch2.S1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=F_{n}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=F_{n}f</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\hat{f}_{0}\\
\hat{f}_{1}\\
\hat{f}_{2}\\
\vdots\\
\hat{f}_{n-1}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\hat{f}_{0}\\
\hat{f}_{1}\\
\hat{f}_{2}\\
\vdots\\
\hat{f}_{n-1}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;1&amp;1&amp;\cdots&amp;1\\
1&amp;\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;\omega^{n-1}\\
1&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{4}&amp;\cdots&amp;\omega^{2(n-1)}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;\omega^{n-1}&amp;\omega^{2(n-1)}&amp;\cdots&amp;\omega^{(n-1)(n-1)}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{2}\\
\vdots\\
f_{n-1}\end{bmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;1&amp;1&amp;\cdots&amp;1\\
1&amp;\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;\omega^{n-1}\\
1&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{4}&amp;\cdots&amp;\omega^{2(n-1)}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;\omega^{n-1}&amp;\omega^{2(n-1)}&amp;\cdots&amp;\omega^{(n-1)(n-1)}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{2}\\
\vdots\\
f_{n-1}\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\omega=\exp\left(-2\pi i/n\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=\exp\left(-2\pi i/n\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is the primitive <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>th root of unity. Note that this makes <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> a complex matrix. This operation is <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> when implemented naively, but can be brought down to <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> using a divide-and-conquer approach: the fast Fourier transform (FFT).</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch2.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02206v1/roots-of-unity.svg" id="Ch2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:191/191;" width="191" height="191"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.02206v1/dft.png" id="Ch2.F2.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:262/197;" width="262" height="197" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2.2</span>: </span><span id="Ch2.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Symmetries of the discrete Fourier transform. (Left) Roots of unity in the complex plane. (Right) Structure of the DFT matrix illustrating periodicity and symmetry.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To get an intuition, let us examine the case <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=4</annotation></semantics></math> first. Equation (<a href="#Ch2.Ex1" title="In 2.1.3 Discrete Fourier Transform ‣ 2.1 Signal Processing ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.11</span></a>) expresses <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and powers of <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=-i</annotation></semantics></math>. We want to “divide” this problem, and express it in terms of the DFT for <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math>, that uses powers of <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{2}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{2}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch2.S1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\hat{f}_{0}\\
\hat{f}_{1}\\
\hat{f}_{2}\\
\hat{f}_{3}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\hat{f}_{0}\\
\hat{f}_{1}\\
\hat{f}_{2}\\
\hat{f}_{3}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;1&amp;1&amp;1\\
1&amp;\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{3}\\
1&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{4}&amp;\omega^{6}\\
1&amp;\omega^{3}&amp;\omega^{6}&amp;\omega^{9}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{2}\\
f_{3}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;1&amp;1&amp;1\\
1&amp;\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{3}\\
1&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{4}&amp;\omega^{6}\\
1&amp;\omega^{3}&amp;\omega^{6}&amp;\omega^{9}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{2}\\
f_{3}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{3}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{3}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{1}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{2}\\
f_{3}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{3}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{3}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{1}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{2}\\
f_{3}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{($\omega^{4}=1$)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{($\omega^{4}=1$)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Observe that <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> exhibits a very clear structure. Row <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> starts with <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which gets multiplied by <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> repeatedly. The key step is realizing that if we take every other element from each row, we will get <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. This makes a lot of sense, because we are just walking the unit circle clockwise twice as fast. We can express this as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch2.S1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\hat{f}_{0}\\
\hat{f}_{1}\\
\hat{f}_{2}\\
\hat{f}_{3}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\hat{f}_{0}\\
\hat{f}_{1}\\
\hat{f}_{2}\\
\hat{f}_{3}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{3}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{2}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{3}&amp;\omega^{1}\\
\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{2}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{3}\\
\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{3}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{2}\\
\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{3}&amp;\omega^{1}\\
\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{2}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{3}\\
\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}F_{2}&amp;\begin{array}[]{cc}\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}\\
\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{3}\end{array}\\
F_{2}&amp;\begin{array}[]{cc}\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{2}\\
\omega^{3}&amp;\omega^{1}\end{array}\end{bmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}F_{2}&amp;\begin{array}[]{cc}\omega^{0}&amp;\omega^{0}\\
\omega^{1}&amp;\omega^{3}\end{array}\\
F_{2}&amp;\begin{array}[]{cc}\omega^{2}&amp;\omega^{2}\\
\omega^{3}&amp;\omega^{1}\end{array}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">What about the remaining columns? They will be like <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, but each row will be offset by increasing powers of <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{2}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{2}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can re-write this sequence as <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\omega^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\omega^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\omega^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\omega^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, we obtain that</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch2.S1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\hat{f}_{0}\\
\hat{f}_{1}\\
\hat{f}_{2}\\
\hat{f}_{3}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}F_{2}&amp;D_{2}F_{2}\\
F_{2}&amp;-D_{2}F_{2}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{2}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{3}\\
\end{bmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\hat{f}_{0}\\
\hat{f}_{1}\\
\hat{f}_{2}\\
\hat{f}_{3}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}F_{2}&amp;D_{2}F_{2}\\
F_{2}&amp;-D_{2}F_{2}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{0}\\
f_{2}\\
f_{1}\\
f_{3}\\
\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> just multiplies each row by increasing factors of <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;0\\
0&amp;\omega\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>ω</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;0\\
0&amp;\omega\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Notice that there was nothing special about <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=4</annotation></semantics></math>, and we can apply the same reasoning to conclude that if <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is a power of two,</p>
<table id="Ch2.S1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}F_{n/2}&amp;D_{n/2}F_{n/2}\\
F_{n/2}&amp;-D_{n/2}F_{n/2}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{\text{even}}\\
f_{\text{odd}}\\
\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>even</mtext></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>odd</mtext></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}F_{n/2}&amp;D_{n/2}F_{n/2}\\
F_{n/2}&amp;-D_{n/2}F_{n/2}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}f_{\text{even}}\\
f_{\text{odd}}\\
\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}F_{n/2}f_{\text{even}}+D_{n/2}F_{n/2}f_{\text{odd}}\\
F_{n/2}f_{\text{even}}-D_{n/2}F_{n/2}f_{\text{odd}}\\
\end{bmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>even</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>odd</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>even</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>odd</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}F_{n/2}f_{\text{even}}+D_{n/2}F_{n/2}f_{\text{odd}}\\
F_{n/2}f_{\text{even}}-D_{n/2}F_{n/2}f_{\text{odd}}\\
\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="Ch2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n/2}=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
0&amp;\omega&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\omega^{n/2-1}\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>ω</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n/2}=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
0&amp;\omega&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\omega^{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\omega^{n/2-1}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">This involves two operations: evaluating two DFTs on inputs that are half the size, and combining those results (which is linear because <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n/2}</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonal). Using the master theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, we easily obtain that the runtime of the fast Fourier transform is <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n\log n)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that because of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 2.1.3 Discrete Fourier Transform ‣ 2.1 Signal Processing ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we can also compute the inverse Fourier transform in <math id="Ch2.S1.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1.4 </span>The Convolution Theorem</h4>

<div id="Thmdefinition7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Circular Convolution)<span id="Thmdefinition7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,g\in\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,g\in\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Their circular convolution is given by</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f*g)_{k}=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}f_{j}g_{k-j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f*g)_{k}=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}f_{j}g_{k-j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the indexes are taken modulo <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Performing a convolution naively requires <math id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> operations. The following theorem will allow us to compute the convolution in the frequency domain in linear time. If we also consider the run-time of the FFT (and the inverse FFT), we conclude that convolutions can be computed in <math id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Convolution Theorem)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Convolution in the time domain corresponds to point-wise multiplication in the frequency domain:</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f*g}=\hat{f}\cdot\hat{g}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f*g}=\hat{f}\cdot\hat{g}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note: <math id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> “wraps-around”, so <math id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> would be <math id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> for example.</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\widehat{f*g})_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\widehat{f*g})_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}(f*g)_{j}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}(f*g)_{j}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\sum_{l=0}^{n-1}f_{l}g_{j-l}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\sum_{l=0}^{n-1}f_{l}g_{j-l}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{l=0}^{n-1}f_{l}\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}g_{j-l}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{l=0}^{n-1}f_{l}\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}g_{j-l}\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{l=0}^{n-1}f_{l}\sum_{m=0}^{n-1}g_{m}\exp\left(-ik(l+m)\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{l=0}^{n-1}f_{l}\sum_{m=0}^{n-1}g_{m}\exp\left(-ik(l+m)\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{l=0}^{n-1}f_{l}\exp\left(-ikl\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)\sum_{m=0}^{n-1}g_{m}\exp\left(-ikm\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{l=0}^{n-1}f_{l}\exp\left(-ikl\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)\sum_{m=0}^{n-1}g_{m}\exp\left(-ikm\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\hat{f}_{k}\cdot\hat{g}_{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\hat{f}_{k}\cdot\hat{g}_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S1.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1.5 </span>Short-Time Fourier Transform</h4>

<div id="Ch2.S1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Fourier transform, and by extension the discrete Fourier transform, provides a frequency representation of an entire signal. However, many signals, particularly audio, are non-stationary, meaning their frequency content changes over time. For instance, in speech, different phonemes have different frequency characteristics, and in music, notes and chords change over time. Applying a single Fourier transform over the entire duration of such a signal would average out these temporal variations, losing critical information. The core idea of the short-time Fourier transform is to break the signal into short segments, and compute the FFT for each segment, thus capturing how the frequency content changes over time. A similar technique, the modified discrete cosine transform (MDCT), is widely used for audio compression.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch2.S1.SS5.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">The Need for Windowing</h5>

<div id="Ch2.S1.SS5.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS5.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When we extract a segment (or “frame”) from a longer signal to analyze its local frequency content using the DFT, we are implicitly assuming that this finite segment represents one period of an infinitely periodic signal. If the extracted segment is simply truncated (i.e., cut abruptly at its ends, which is equivalent to applying a rectangular window), sharp discontinuities can be created at the boundaries of this implied periodic repetition.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS5.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS5.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These discontinuities lead to a phenomenon called spectral leakage. In the frequency domain, this results in energy from the true frequency component “leaking” into adjacent frequency bins. To mitigate this, we apply a window function to each segment before computing its FFT. The window function is often zero or near-zero at the ends of the segment, which reduces discontinuities. See Figure <a href="#Ch2.F3" title="Figure 2.3 ‣ The Need for Windowing ‣ 2.1.5 Short-Time Fourier Transform ‣ 2.1 Signal Processing ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> for a visual explanation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch2.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Ch2.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02206v1/window-square-good.svg" id="Ch2.F3.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F3.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="Ch2.F3.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Rectangular window (whole number of periods)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Ch2.F3.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02206v1/window-square-bad.svg" id="Ch2.F3.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F3.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="Ch2.F3.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Rectangular window (fractional number of periods)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Ch2.F3.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02206v1/window-hanning.svg" id="Ch2.F3.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F3.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="Ch2.F3.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Hahn window (fractional number of periods)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2.3</span>: </span><span id="Ch2.F3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Effect of windowing on the STFT.<span id="Ch2.F3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Figure (a) shows a signal with exactly five periods of a sine wave, where the start and end points align smoothly. As a result, the DFT clearly identifies the 5 Hz frequency. In Figure (b), the signal contains five and a half periods, and the endpoints do not match. This causes spectral leakage, spreading power into neighboring frequency bins beyond just 5 and 6 Hz. In Figure (c), the signal is multiplied by a Hann window, which reduces the discontinuities at the boundaries. Consequently, the magnitude spectrum becomes more concentrated around the 5 and 6 Hz components.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Thmdefinition8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 8</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Discrete short-time Fourier transform)<span id="Thmdefinition8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let</span></p>
<ul id="Ch2.S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch2.S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathbb{C}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathbb{C}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a signal</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the window size (or frame length)</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a window function</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the “hop-size” (often </span><math id="Ch2.S1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n}{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> or </span><math id="Ch2.S1.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n}{4}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">)</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then we can define</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}_{m,k}=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}w_{j}\cdot f_{j+mh}\cdot\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}_{m,k}=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}w_{j}\cdot f_{j+mh}\cdot\exp\left(-ikj\frac{2\pi}{n}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition8.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<ul id="Ch2.S1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch2.S1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> ranges from </span><math id="Ch2.S1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="Ch2.S1.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lfloor\frac{S-n}{h}\right\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lfloor\frac{S-n}{h}\right\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> ranges from </span><math id="Ch2.S1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S1.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="Ch2.S1.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS5.SSSx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS5.SSSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">There are two important hyperparameters here, the frame length <math id="Ch2.S1.SS5.SSSx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and the hop-size <math id="Ch2.S1.SS5.SSSx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. The frame length introduces a time-frequency trade-off: larger values will result in good frequency resolution, while small values will provide good time localization.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1.6 </span>Mel-spectrograms</h4>

<div id="Ch2.S1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The short-time Fourier transform of an audio signal yields a complex-valued matrix, with time along the x-axis and frequency along the y-axis. For visualization purposes, we typically extract the magnitude (or power) of each complex number and discard the phase. This is not because phase is unimportant (it is needed to reconstruct the signal) but because phase spectrograms often appear noisy and unstructured (see Figure <a href="#Ch2.F4" title="Figure 2.4 ‣ 2.1.6 Mel-spectrograms ‣ 2.1 Signal Processing ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Humans do not perceive frequency on a linear scale. In particular, we are more sensitive to changes at lower frequencies than at higher ones. To model this, the mel scale was introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>. The mel scale maps frequency (in Hz) to a perceptual scale (mels) where equal intervals correspond to equal perceived pitch differences. Although the mel scale was empirically derived from perceptual experiments, some researchers have proposed formulas to convert <math id="Ch2.S1.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> hertz into <math id="Ch2.S1.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> mels, such as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="Ch2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2595\log_{10}\left(1+\frac{f}{700}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2595</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>700</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2595\log_{10}\left(1+\frac{f}{700}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="Ch2.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Ch2.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02206v1/wave.svg" id="Ch2.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/358;" width="476" height="358"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F4.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="Ch2.F4.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Original waveform</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Ch2.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.02206v1/phase.png" id="Ch2.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F4.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="Ch2.F4.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Phase of the STFT</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Ch2.F4.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.02206v1/magnitude.png" id="Ch2.F4.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F4.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="Ch2.F4.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Magnitude of the STFT</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="Ch2.F4.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.02206v1/magnitude-mel.png" id="Ch2.F4.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F4.sf4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(d)</span> </span><span id="Ch2.F4.sf4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mel-spectrogram</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch2.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2.4</span>: </span><span id="Ch2.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">In (a) we see a waveform that corresponds to a one-second utterance from the SC09 dataset (see Section <a href="#Ch4.S1" title="4.1 Datasets ‣ Chapter 4 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>). After applying the short-term Fourier transform (STFT), we get a complex-valued matrix. The phase (b) seems quite random, but the magnitude (c) is very structured. Finally, (d) shows the mel-spectrogram.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S2" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2.2 </span>Metrics</h3>

<div id="Ch2.S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For training, we maximize the log-likelihood of the ground-truth sequence <math id="Ch2.S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> under the model’s predicted distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 9</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Log-likelihood)<span id="Thmdefinition9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a ground-truth sequence <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(x_{1},\dots,x_{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(x_{1},\dots,x_{S})</annotation></semantics></math>, and a model <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x_{&lt;k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x_{&lt;k})</annotation></semantics></math>, the log-likelihood is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\LL(x;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>LL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\LL(x;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log_{2}\left(\prod_{k=1}^{S}P_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\mid x_{&lt;k}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log_{2}\left(\prod_{k=1}^{S}P_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\mid x_{&lt;k}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{S}\log_{2}P_{\theta}(x_{k}\mid x_{&lt;k})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{S}\log_{2}P_{\theta}(x_{k}\mid x_{&lt;k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In order to evaluate our model, we use the log-likelihood on a held-out test dataset. In addition, and following prior literature, we also compute the FID and IS scores on samples generated by the model. In the generative case, we could compute <math id="Ch2.S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\LL(x;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>LL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\LL(x;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> with samples instead of with the ground truth. However, this approach fails to capture sample diversity, as the model could repeatedly generate the same output. To better evaluate both the quality and diversity of the generated samples, we use the following procedure:</p>
<ol id="Ch2.S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Ch2.S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Train a classifier on the raw data.</span> For example, in the SC09 dataset (see Section <a href="#Ch4.S1" title="4.1 Datasets ‣ Chapter 4 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>), we can classify each utterance into ten different digits using mel-spectrograms. In ImageNet, we can do 1000-class classification.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Use the activations of the classifier</span>. Two audio recordings that are semantically similar can be quite different in wave space. Because of this, we use some activations of the classifier. For example, the IS score uses the model’s output probability distribution, and the FID score uses the last layer activations to compare the training samples with the generated ones.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Ch2.S2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Before we dive into the specific metrics, we should mention some of their limitations. First, they heavily rely on the accuracy of the pre-trained classifier. Second, they assess the generated samples through a proxy, which might not fully align with human perception. Finally, these metrics might ignore low-level details, potentially allowing artifacts to go unnoticed.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch2.S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2.1 </span>IS score</h4>

<div id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Inception Score <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> was introduced in 2016 to evaluate the image quality of Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs). The classifier used was Inception v3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> (thus the name), and the activations used are the outputs of the model after the softmax layer.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 10</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The IS score is defined as</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ln\IS" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>IS</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ln\IS</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E33.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX[\KL(p(\cdot\mid X)\mid\mid\EX[p(\cdot\mid X)])]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX[\KL(p(\cdot\mid X)\mid\mid\EX[p(\cdot\mid X)])]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX_{x\sim\text{samples}}\left[\KL(p(\cdot\mid x)\mid\mid\EX_{x^{\prime}\sim\text{samples}}[p(\cdot\mid x^{\prime})])\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">samples</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">samples</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX_{x\sim\text{samples}}\left[\KL(p(\cdot\mid x)\mid\mid\EX_{x^{\prime}\sim\text{samples}}[p(\cdot\mid x^{\prime})])\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability distribution outputted by the classifier given <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let us enumerate first some useful facts, that will be then proven.</p>
<ul id="Ch2.S2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch2.S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We want to <span id="Ch2.S2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">maximize</span> the IS score.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The IS score ranges between 1 (worst) and <math id="Ch2.S2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (best), the number of classes of the classifier.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A score of one corresponds to the classifier always making the same prediction. This is bad because samples are not diverse.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A score of <math id="Ch2.S2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> means that the samples are evenly spread across all classes (good diversity) and that the classifier is always certain about its predictions (generated samples are sharp and distinct).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The IS score is always greater or equal to one</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the KL divergence is always non-negative, <math id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln(\IS)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>IS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln(\IS)</annotation></semantics></math> will never be negative. By exponentiating, we get that <math id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\IS\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>IS</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\IS\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The IS score is bounded by <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and the bound is achieved when</span></p>
<ul id="Ch2.S2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch2.S2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EX[p(\cdot\mid X)]_{k}=\frac{1}{K}\quad\forall k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EX[p(\cdot\mid X)]_{k}=\frac{1}{K}\quad\forall k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (samples spread across all classes)</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot\mid X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot\mid X)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ch2.S2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is one-hot (classifier is certain about its predictions)</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Y=p(\cdot\mid X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=p(\cdot\mid X)</annotation></semantics></math> for clarity.</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ln\IS" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>IS</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ln\IS</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX[\KL(p(\cdot\mid X)\mid\mid\EX[p(\cdot\mid X)])]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX[\KL(p(\cdot\mid X)\mid\mid\EX[p(\cdot\mid X)])]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX[\KL(Y\mid\mid\EX[Y])]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX[\KL(Y\mid\mid\EX[Y])]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}y_{k}\log\left(\frac{y_{k}}{\EX[Y]_{k}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}y_{k}\log\left(\frac{y_{k}}{\EX[Y]_{k}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}y_{k}\log(y_{k})\right]-\EX\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}y_{k}\log(\EX[Y]_{k})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}y_{k}\log(y_{k})\right]-\EX\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}y_{k}\log(\EX[Y]_{k})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\EX[H(Y)]-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\EX[Y]_{k}\log(\EX[Y]_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\EX[H(Y)]-\sum_{k=1}^{K}\EX[Y]_{k}\log(\EX[Y]_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E39.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(definition of Entropy)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\EX[H(Y)]+H(\EX[Y])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\EX[H(Y)]+H(\EX[Y])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E40.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(definition of Entropy)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log(K)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log(K).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E41.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Entropy is bounded from 0 to <math id="Ch2.E41.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(K)</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We can just take exponentials on both sides to get the required bound. Let us now show that the bound can be achieved. If <math id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EX[Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EX[Y]</annotation></semantics></math> is uniform (samples are uniformly spread across all classes), <math id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\EX[Y])=\log(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\EX[Y])=\log(K)</annotation></semantics></math>. If the classifier is completely certain about its predictions, <math id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> will be one-hot, so <math id="Ch2.S2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EX[H(Y)]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EX[H(Y)]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2.2 </span>FID score</h4>

<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Fréchet Inception Distance (FID) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>, introduced in 2017, was designed to overcome a key limitation of the Inception Score (IS): IS does not take into account the statistics of the real data distribution. FID addresses this by modeling both the real and generated samples as multivariate Gaussian distributions and comparing them using the Fréchet distance. Unlike the IS, where higher values are better, lower FID scores indicate that the samples are similar to the training data.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To make this comparison meaningful, samples are not evaluated in their raw form (e.g., waveform for audio or pixel space for images), but rather through their representations in a semantically rich space (the activations from the final layer of a pre-trained classifier).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 11</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Fréchet distance between two probability distributions <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(P,Q)^{2}=\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX[\left\lVert X-Y\right\rVert^{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(P,Q)^{2}=\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX[\left\lVert X-Y\right\rVert^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We can define <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(P,Q)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(P,Q)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the centered variables <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}=X-\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}=X-\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Y}=Y-\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Y}=Y-\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(P,Q)^{2}=\left\lVert\mu-\mu^{\prime}\right\rVert^{2}+\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX\left[\left\lVert\hat{X}-\hat{Y}\right\rVert^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(P,Q)^{2}=\left\lVert\mu-\mu^{\prime}\right\rVert^{2}+\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX\left[\left\lVert\hat{X}-\hat{Y}\right\rVert^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch2.S2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert X-Y\right\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert X-Y\right\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle X-Y,X-Y\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle X-Y,X-Y\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle\hat{X}-\hat{Y}+\mu-\mu^{\prime},\hat{X}-\hat{Y}+\mu-\mu^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle\hat{X}-\hat{Y}+\mu-\mu^{\prime},\hat{X}-\hat{Y}+\mu-\mu^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\lVert\hat{X}-\hat{Y}\right\rVert^{2}+\left\lVert\mu-\mu^{\prime}\right\rVert^{2}+2\langle\hat{X}-\hat{Y},\mu-\mu^{\prime}\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\lVert\hat{X}-\hat{Y}\right\rVert^{2}+\left\lVert\mu-\mu^{\prime}\right\rVert^{2}+2\langle\hat{X}-\hat{Y},\mu-\mu^{\prime}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that the third term will cancel after taking expectations, because the expected value of the centered variables is zero. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d(P,Q)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d(P,Q)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX[\left\lVert X-Y\right\rVert^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX[\left\lVert X-Y\right\rVert^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\lVert\mu-\mu^{\prime}\right\rVert^{2}+\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX\left[\left\lVert\hat{X}-\hat{Y}\right\rVert^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\lVert\mu-\mu^{\prime}\right\rVert^{2}+\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX\left[\left\lVert\hat{X}-\hat{Y}\right\rVert^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmproposition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EX[\left\lVert Z\right\rVert^{2}]=\Tr(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EX[\left\lVert Z\right\rVert^{2}]=\Tr(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch2.S2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EX[\left\lVert Z\right\rVert^{2}]=\EX\left[\sum_{i}Z_{i}^{2}\right]=\sum_{i}\EX[Z_{i}^{2}]=\sum_{i}\Var(Z_{i})=\Tr(\Sigma)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EX[\left\lVert Z\right\rVert^{2}]=\EX\left[\sum_{i}Z_{i}^{2}\right]=\sum_{i}\EX[Z_{i}^{2}]=\sum_{i}\Var(Z_{i})=\Tr(\Sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=\mathcal{N}(\mu,\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=\mathcal{N}(\mu,\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\mathcal{N}(\mu^{\prime},\Sigma^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\mathcal{N}(\mu^{\prime},\Sigma^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> invertible. Then,</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(P,Q)^{2}=\left\lVert\mu-\mu^{\prime}\right\rVert^{2}+\Tr\left(\Sigma+\Sigma^{\prime}-2\sqrt{\sqrt{\Sigma}\Sigma^{\prime}\sqrt{\Sigma}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msqrt></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(P,Q)^{2}=\left\lVert\mu-\mu^{\prime}\right\rVert^{2}+\Tr\left(\Sigma+\Sigma^{\prime}-2\sqrt{\sqrt{\Sigma}\Sigma^{\prime}\sqrt{\Sigma}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We will use <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 2.2.2 FID score ‣ 2.2 Metrics ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> to assume without loss of generality that <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> are centered around zero. Thus, we have</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d(P,Q)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d(P,Q)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX[\left\lVert X-Y\right\rVert^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\EX[\left\lVert X-Y\right\rVert^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E51.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(<a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 2.2.2 FID score ‣ 2.2 Metrics ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\Tr(\Cov(X-Y))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\Tr(\Cov(X-Y)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E52.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(<a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 2.2.2 FID score ‣ 2.2 Metrics ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X-Y=\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;-I\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}X\\
Y\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>X</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>Y</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X-Y=\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;-I\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}X\\
Y\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Cov(X-Y)=\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;-I\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Sigma&amp;C\\
C^{T}&amp;\Sigma^{\prime}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}I\\
-I\end{bmatrix}=\Sigma+\Sigma^{\prime}-C-C^{T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>C</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Cov(X-Y)=\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;-I\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Sigma&amp;C\\
C^{T}&amp;\Sigma^{\prime}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}I\\
-I\end{bmatrix}=\Sigma+\Sigma^{\prime}-C-C^{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is the cross-covariance matrix. Thus, we have to</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\Tr\left(\Sigma+\Sigma^{\prime}-C-C^{T}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{X\sim P,Y\sim Q}\Tr\left(\Sigma+\Sigma^{\prime}-C-C^{T}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed, and <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Tr C=\Tr C^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Tr C=\Tr C^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, so we just have to maximize <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Tr C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Tr C</annotation></semantics></math> under the constraint that <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Cov(X-Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Cov(X-Y)</annotation></semantics></math> should be positive semi-definite:</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\Cov(X-Y)\succeq 0}\Tr C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\Cov(X-Y)\succeq 0}\Tr C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">Because of Schur’s condition for positive definiteness,</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Cov(X-Y)=\begin{bmatrix}\Sigma&amp;C\\
C^{T}&amp;\Sigma^{\prime}\end{bmatrix}\succeq 0\quad\iff\quad\Sigma^{\prime}-C^{T}\Sigma^{-1}C\succeq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>C</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Cov(X-Y)=\begin{bmatrix}\Sigma&amp;C\\
C^{T}&amp;\Sigma^{\prime}\end{bmatrix}\succeq 0\quad\iff\quad\Sigma^{\prime}-C^{T}\Sigma^{-1}C\succeq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">Now we will substitute <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\sqrt{\Sigma}K\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\sqrt{\Sigma}K\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we can do because both <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are invertible. While this might seem a bit obscure at first, it will greatly simplify things:</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma^{\prime}-C^{T}\Sigma^{-1}C\succeq 0\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma^{\prime}-C^{T}\Sigma^{-1}C\succeq 0\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E58.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\iff\quad\Sigma^{\prime}-\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}K^{T}K\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt><mi>K</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>K</mi><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff\quad\Sigma^{\prime}-\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}K^{T}K\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\iff\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}(I-K^{T}K)\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}(I-K^{T}K)\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\iff\quad(I-K^{T}K)\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff\quad(I-K^{T}K)\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E60.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(congruent transformation)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\iff\quad\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff\quad\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E61.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(spectral norm definition)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">Our problem is now</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left({\sqrt{\Sigma}K\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left({\sqrt{\Sigma}K\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.9.1" class="ltx_text">So,</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left({\sqrt{\Sigma}K\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left({\sqrt{\Sigma}K\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left(K\underbrace{{\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}\sqrt{\Sigma}}}_{A}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>A</mi></munder></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left(K\underbrace{{\sqrt{\Sigma^{\prime}}\sqrt{\Sigma}}}_{A}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E63.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(cyclic property of the trace)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left(KUDV^{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left(KUDV^{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E64.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(SVD decomposition of <math id="Ch2.E64.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left(\underbrace{V^{T}KU}_{M}D\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>M</mi></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\Tr\left(\underbrace{V^{T}KU}_{M}D\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E65.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(cyclic property of the trace)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\sum_{i}M_{ii}D_{ii}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1}\sum_{i}M_{ii}D_{ii}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E66.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(definition of trace)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i}D_{ii}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i}D_{ii}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E67.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(norm is unitarily invariant, so <math id="Ch2.E67.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert M\right\rVert\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert M\right\rVert\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Tr(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Tr(D)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E68.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(definition of trace)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Tr(\sqrt{A^{T}A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Tr(\sqrt{A^{T}A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Ch2.E69.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(<math id="Ch2.E69.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=UDV^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=UDV^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="Ch2.E69.m2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{A^{T}A}=VDV^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{A^{T}A}=VDV^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\sqrt{\sqrt{\Sigma}\Sigma^{\prime}\sqrt{\Sigma}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msqrt></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\sqrt{\sqrt{\Sigma}\Sigma^{\prime}\sqrt{\Sigma}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.10.1" class="ltx_text">It is not immediately clear why <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{ii}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{ii}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. However, note that <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert M\right\rVert=\left\lVert V^{T}KU\right\rVert=\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert M\right\rVert=\left\lVert V^{T}KU\right\rVert=\left\lVert K\right\rVert\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.E71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{x^{T}Mx}{x^{T}x}\leq 1\quad\forall x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{x^{T}Mx}{x^{T}x}\leq 1\quad\forall x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.11.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, if we choose <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=e_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=e_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{ii}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{ii}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. We established an upper bound, that can be easily achieved setting <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=I</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the same as choosing <math id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=VU^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=VU^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S2.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S3" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2.3 </span>Sequence-to-sequence models</h3>

<div id="Ch2.S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to maximize the log-likelihood, so we need a model that receives a variable number of tokens <math id="Ch2.S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},...,x_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},...,x_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and outputs <math id="Ch2.S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(x_{k}\mid x_{&lt;k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(x_{k}\mid x_{&lt;k})</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, we will focus on sequence-to-sequence models, whose inputs and outputs have shape <math id="Ch2.S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B,S,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B,S,D)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ch2.S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> represents the batch size, <math id="Ch2.S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> the sequence length and <math id="Ch2.S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> the feature dimension. The tensor <span id="Ch2.S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">output[:, k, :]</span> is used to compute the conditional probability <math id="Ch2.S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(x_{k}\mid x_{&lt;k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(x_{k}\mid x_{&lt;k})</annotation></semantics></math>, as required by Equation (<a href="#Ch2.E31" title="Equation 2.31 ‣ Definition 9 (Log-likelihood). ‣ 2.2 Metrics ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.31</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These models are composed of several blocks, each of which receives and outputs tensors of shape <math id="Ch2.S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B,S,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B,S,D)</annotation></semantics></math>. There are two kinds of blocks that alternate:</p>
<ol id="Ch2.S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Channel mixing.</span> This is typically done with multilayer perceptron (MLPs), that require</p>
<ul id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(D^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(D^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> parameters</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S3.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(BSD^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(BSD^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> matmul flops</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch2.S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Temporal mixing,</span> which mixes the activations across the time dimension. The complexity of this block depends on the layer used.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As we will see in the next section, temporal mixing is <math id="Ch2.S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(BSD^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(BSD^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> if we use recurrent neural networks, or <math id="Ch2.S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(BS^{2}D+BSD^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(BS^{2}D+BSD^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is we use self-attention. Thus, if <math id="Ch2.S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\gg S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\gg S</annotation></semantics></math> (very often the case), it is perfectly reasonable to use self-attention. However, if we are dealing with very long sequences, recurrent networks are preferred, since they are linear with the sequence length.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3.1 </span>Recurrent neural networks</h4>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recurrent neural networks process data sequentially, keeping some sort of state. In each time-step, the output <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and the new state are computed based on the current input <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and state. We will now review several recurrent neural networks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="Ch2.T1.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="Ch2.T1.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch2.T1.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch2.T1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="Ch2.T1.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch2.T1.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameters</span></th>
<th id="Ch2.T1.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch2.T1.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Matmul flops</span></th>
<th id="Ch2.T1.3.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch2.T1.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Element-wise flops</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="Ch2.T1.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch2.T1.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Elman RNN</th>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="Ch2.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3D^{2}+2D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3D^{2}+2D</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="Ch2.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6BSD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6BSD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="Ch2.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5BSD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5BSD</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="Ch2.T1.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch2.T1.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">LSTM</th>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8D^{2}+4D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8D^{2}+4D</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16BSD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16BSD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="17BSD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>17</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">17BSD</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="Ch2.T1.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch2.T1.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">GRU</th>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6D^{2}+3D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6D^{2}+3D</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12BSD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12BSD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="14BSD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14BSD</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="Ch2.T1.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch2.T1.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b">RG-LRU</th>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><math id="Ch2.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2D^{2}+3D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2D^{2}+3D</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><math id="Ch2.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4BSD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4BSD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Ch2.T1.3.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><math id="Ch2.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13BSD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13BSD</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Ch2.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2.1</span>: </span><span id="Ch2.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Complexity of recurrent neural network layers in terms of the batch size (B), the sequence length (S), and the number of channels (D). Note: multiplying a matrix and a vector requires <math id="Ch2.T1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(2D-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(2D-1)</annotation></semantics></math> operations (<math id="Ch2.T1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> multiplications and <math id="Ch2.T1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D-1</annotation></semantics></math> sums are required for every output).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Elman network</h5>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An Elman network <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> uses a single vector to keep track of the state.</p>
<table id="Ch2.S3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma\left(W_{h}x_{k}+U_{h}h_{k-1}+b_{h}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma\left(W_{h}x_{k}+U_{h}h_{k-1}+b_{h}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E73.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma\left(W_{y}h_{k}+b_{y}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma\left(W_{y}h_{k}+b_{y}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the logistic function <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x)\coloneq 1/(1+\exp(-x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x)\coloneq 1/(1+\exp(-x))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">LSTM</h5>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The long short-term memory unit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> was designed to mitigate the vanishing gradient problem. The state is comprised of two different vectors, the cell state <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and the hidden state <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="Ch2.S3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{f}x_{k}+U_{f}h_{k-1}+b_{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{f}x_{k}+U_{f}h_{k-1}+b_{f})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{i}x_{k}+U_{i}h_{k-1}+b_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{i}x_{k}+U_{i}h_{k-1}+b_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle o_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{o}x_{k}+U_{o}h_{k-1}+b_{o})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{o}x_{k}+U_{o}h_{k-1}+b_{o})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tanh(W_{c}x_{k}+U_{c}h_{k-1}+b_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tanh(W_{c}x_{k}+U_{c}h_{k-1}+b_{c})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E78.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{k}\odot c_{k-1}+i_{k}\odot\tilde{c}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{k}\odot c_{k-1}+i_{k}\odot\tilde{c}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E79.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=o_{k}\odot\tanh(c_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=o_{k}\odot\tanh(c_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">GRU</h5>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The gated recurrent unit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> is similar to an LSTM, but the state is comprised of just one vector. It also requires fewer parameters.</p>
<table id="Ch2.S3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{z}x_{k}+U_{z}h_{k-1}+b_{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{z}x_{k}+U_{z}h_{k-1}+b_{z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E83.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{r}x_{k}+U_{r}h_{k-1}+b_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{r}x_{k}+U_{r}h_{k-1}+b_{r})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{h}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{h}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tanh(W_{h}x_{k}+U_{h}(r_{k}\odot h_{k-1})+b_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tanh(W_{h}x_{k}+U_{h}(r_{k}\odot h_{k-1})+b_{h})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E85.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-z_{k})\odot h_{k-1}+z_{k}\odot\hat{h}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-z_{k})\odot h_{k-1}+z_{k}\odot\hat{h}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">RG-LRU</h5>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The real-gated linear recurrent unit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> can be expressed as <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}=M(x)h_{k-1}+c(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}=M(x)h_{k-1}+c(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. As we will explain in the state-space models section, this is crucial to parallelize the computation. In addition, it incorporates a gating mechanism, inspired by LSTMs and GRUs.</p>
<table id="Ch2.S3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E86.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{a}x_{k}+b_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{a}x_{k}+b_{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E87.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{x}x_{k}+b_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(W_{x}x_{k}+b_{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a^{cr_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a^{cr_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E89.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a_{k}\odot h_{k-1}+\sqrt{1-a_{k}^{2}}\odot(i_{k}\odot x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a_{k}\odot h_{k-1}+\sqrt{1-a_{k}^{2}}\odot(i_{k}\odot x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> can be parametrized as <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\Lambda)\exp(i\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\Lambda)\exp(i\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda,\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{D}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda,\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{D}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This guarantees that <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\left\lVert a_{k}\right\rVert\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\left\lVert a_{k}\right\rVert\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="Ch2.S3.SS1.SSSx4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is usually set to a scalar-valued constant.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3.2 </span>Self-attention</h4>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> revolutionized the field of natural language processing by introducing the attention mechanism, that allows each token to attend to other tokens in the sequence. This contrasts with recurrent neural networks, that only have access to the current token and a compressed representation of the past (hidden state).</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We will now give a brief explanation of the multi-head self-attention mechanism. Let <math id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sample within a batch. A self-attention layer will take <math id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and output <math id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="Ch2.S3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we compute <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,k,v\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times H\times\frac{D}{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,k,v\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times H\times\frac{D}{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> stand for queries, keys, and values, respectively. <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of “heads”, a hyperparameter. This requires</p>
<ul id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> parameters</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6BSD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6BSD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> matmul flops</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute the attention matrix <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times S\times H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times S\times H}</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="Ch2.E90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ijh}=\frac{\exp\left(\tilde{a}_{ijh}\right)}{\sum\limits_{j^{\prime}=1}^{S}\exp\left(\tilde{a}_{ij^{\prime}h}\right)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ijh}=\frac{\exp\left(\tilde{a}_{ijh}\right)}{\sum\limits_{j^{\prime}=1}^{S}\exp\left(\tilde{a}_{ij^{\prime}h}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="Ch2.E91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{a}_{ijh}=\frac{\langle q_{ih:},k_{jh:}\rangle}{\sqrt{D/H}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{a}_{ijh}=\frac{\langle q_{ih:},k_{jh:}\rangle}{\sqrt{D/H}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In the autoregressive setting, the unnormalized tensor <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{a}</annotation></semantics></math> is modified by setting <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{a}_{ijh}=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{a}_{ijh}=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math> to prevent tokens from attending to the future. This requires</p>
<ul id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No parameters</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2BS^{2}D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2BS^{2}D</annotation></semantics></math> matmul flops</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute the output of each attention head by applying the attention weights to the values. This yields a tensor <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times H\times\frac{D}{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times H\times\frac{D}{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where:</p>
<table id="Ch2.E92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{ihd}=\sum_{j=1}^{S}a_{ijh}v_{jhd}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{ihd}=\sum_{j=1}^{S}a_{ijh}v_{jhd}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This step requires:</p>
<ul id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No parameters</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2BS^{2}D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2BS^{2}D</annotation></semantics></math> matmul flops</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we concatenate the outputs of all <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> heads and apply a linear projection to produce the output <math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>. This step requires:</p>
<ul id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> parameters</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch2.S3.I2.i4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2BSD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2BSD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> matmul flops</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the number of matmul flops is <math id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(BSD^{2}+BS^{2}D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(BSD^{2}+BS^{2}D)</annotation></semantics></math>, so it is quadratic both in the model’s dimension, and in the sequence length. In many real world cases, <math id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\ll D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\ll D</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, GPT-3 was trained with <math id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2048</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=2048</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=12288" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12288</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=12288</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, so <math id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\ll D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\ll D</annotation></semantics></math>. In this thesis, we focus on the opposite case.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Some modern transformer architectures make use of multi-query attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> instead of multi-head attention, in which the same keys and values are shared across all heads, reducing the size of these tensors. While this results in a significant speedup because of the lower memory requirements, it does not change the quadratic complexity with respect to sequence length.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3.3 </span>State Space Models and Linear RNNs</h4>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">State space models (SSMs) are a class of models originally developed in control theory to describe the evolution of dynamical systems in continuous time. In this framework, the system’s state evolves according to a set of differential equations, and outputs are generated as functions of the state and input. In practice, we discretize these equations to obtain models suitable for digital computation. The resulting discrete-time SSMs are equivalent to recurrent neural networks (RNNs) with linear state transitions. We include the continuous case here for historical context and completeness, but our focus is on the discretized version used in modern sequence modeling.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 12</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Continuous-time SSM)<span id="Thmdefinition12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A state space model is defined by the following equation, that maps an input signal <math id="Thmdefinition12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)</annotation></semantics></math> to a latent state <math id="Thmdefinition12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and an output <math id="Thmdefinition12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Ah(t)+Bx(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Ah(t)+Bx(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E94.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Ch(t)+Dx(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Ch(t)+Dx(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 13</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Discrete-time SSM)<span id="Thmdefinition13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The discrete SSM is given by</span></p>
<table id="Ch2.S3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E96.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\overline{A}h_{k-1}+\overline{B}x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\overline{A}h_{k-1}+\overline{B}x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E97.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\overline{C}h_{k}+\overline{D}x_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\overline{C}h_{k}+\overline{D}x_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{A},\overline{B},\overline{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{A},\overline{B},\overline{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{D}</annotation></semantics></math> depend on both <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B,C,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B,C,D</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> (the time-step).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Discretization</h5>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">How the continuous parameters are transformed into the discrete parameters depends on the discretization rule. Let us briefly go through the zero-order hold method. We will assume that <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is piecewise constant, so <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)=x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)=x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\left[k\Delta,(k+1)\Delta\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\left[k\Delta,(k+1)\Delta\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is not piecewise constant, and that to find it we need to solve the following ODE, where <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> runs from 0 to <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> (for convenience), and <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(0)=h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(0)=h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="Ch2.E98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}(t)=Ah(t)+Bx_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}(t)=Ah(t)+Bx_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As usual with inhomogeneous linear ODEs, we will first find a homogeneous solution (setting <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Bx_{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Bx_{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="Ch2.E99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}(t)=Ah(t)\implies h(t)=\exp(At)c," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}(t)=Ah(t)\implies h(t)=\exp(At)c,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(M)=I+M+\frac{1}{2!}M^{2}+\frac{1}{3!}M^{3}+\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(M)=I+M+\frac{1}{2!}M^{2}+\frac{1}{3!}M^{3}+\cdots</annotation></semantics></math> is the matrix exponential. Then, we find a particular solution (setting <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="Ch2.E100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ah(t)+Bx_{k}=0\implies h(t)=-A^{-1}Bx_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ah(t)+Bx_{k}=0\implies h(t)=-A^{-1}Bx_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, a general solution will be given by</p>
<table id="Ch2.E101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(t)=\exp(At)c-A^{-1}Bx_{k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(t)=\exp(At)c-A^{-1}Bx_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(0)=h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(0)=h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Imposing this yields <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=h_{k}+A^{-1}Bx_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=h_{k}+A^{-1}Bx_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</p>
<table id="Ch2.E102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(t)=\exp(At)\left(h_{k}+A^{-1}Bx_{k}\right)-A^{-1}Bx_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(t)=\exp(At)\left(h_{k}+A^{-1}Bx_{k}\right)-A^{-1}Bx_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and rearranging yields</p>
<table id="Ch2.E103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k+1}=h(\Delta)=\exp(A\Delta)h_{k}+\left(\exp(A\Delta)-I\right)A^{-1}Bx_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k+1}=h(\Delta)=\exp(A\Delta)h_{k}+\left(\exp(A\Delta)-I\right)A^{-1}Bx_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="Ch2.S3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{A}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E104.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp(A\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp(A\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{B}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E105.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\exp(A\Delta)-I\right)A^{-1}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\exp(A\Delta)-I\right)A^{-1}B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Note: in some papers in the literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is placed up front. Naturally, the expressions are identical, because the solution is unique (Picard–Lindelöf theorem). The reason is that <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(A\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(A\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, as the exponential is polynomial in <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">The recurrent view</h5>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The discretized SSM is equivalent to a recurrent neural network, allowing us to easily compute <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(SD^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(SD^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> time. We always use the recurrent view for inference. For training, we can use the recurrent view, the convolutional view, or an associative scan.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">The convolutional view</h5>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The convolutional view can be used to parallelize training. Note that <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> can easily be computed in parallel once we have <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, so let’s focus on <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, which is defined sequentially. The sequence <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a simple recurrent neural network without gating, so we can unroll the recurrence as follows:</p>
<table id="Ch2.S3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch2.E106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E106.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E107.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\overline{B}x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\overline{B}x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E108.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\overline{B}x_{2}+\overline{A}\overline{B}x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\overline{B}x_{2}+\overline{A}\overline{B}x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\overline{B}x_{3}+\overline{A}\overline{B}x_{2}+\overline{A}^{2}\overline{B}x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\overline{B}x_{3}+\overline{A}\overline{B}x_{2}+\overline{A}^{2}\overline{B}x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch2.E111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch2.E111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\overline{A}^{k-i}\overline{B}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\overline{A}^{k-i}\overline{B}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=K*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=K*x</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> denotes convolution (Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition7" title="Definition 7 (Circular Convolution). ‣ 2.1.4 The Convolution Theorem ‣ 2.1 Signal Processing ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), and <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(\overline{B},\overline{A}\overline{B},\overline{A}^{2}\overline{B},...)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(\overline{B},\overline{A}\overline{B},\overline{A}^{2}\overline{B},...)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, given <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> we can compute <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(S\log(S)D^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(S\log(S)D^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> using the FFT (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Convolution Theorem). ‣ 2.1.4 The Convolution Theorem ‣ 2.1 Signal Processing ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). This is slower than the recurrent implementation, but it is <em id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">parallelizable</em>. In particular, with enough devices the parallel FFT can bring the time down to <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log(S)D^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log(S)D^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The biggest problem is that in order to compute <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, we have to multiply <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{A}</annotation></semantics></math> with itself <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> times, which results in a runtime of <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(SD^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(SD^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. One way of speeding this up is by diagonalizing <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us consider the change of basis <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=Vh^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=Vh^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch2.E113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch2.E113.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{\begin{aligned} h_{k}&amp;=\overline{A}h_{k-1}+\overline{B}x_{k}\\
y_{k}&amp;=\overline{C}h_{k}+\overline{D}x_{k}\end{aligned}\right.\,\Rightarrow\,\left\{\begin{aligned} Vh_{k}^{\prime}&amp;=\overline{A}Vh_{k-1}^{\prime}+\overline{B}x_{k}\\
y_{k}&amp;=\overline{C}Vh_{k}^{\prime}+\overline{D}x_{k}\end{aligned}\right.\,\Rightarrow\,\left\{\begin{aligned} h_{k}^{\prime}&amp;=V^{-1}\overline{A}Vh_{k-1}^{\prime}+V^{-1}\overline{B}x_{k}\\
y_{k}&amp;=\overline{C}Vh_{k}^{\prime}+\overline{D}x_{k}\end{aligned}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\begin{aligned} h_{k}&amp;=\overline{A}h_{k-1}+\overline{B}x_{k}\\
y_{k}&amp;=\overline{C}h_{k}+\overline{D}x_{k}\end{aligned}\right.\,\Rightarrow\,\left\{\begin{aligned} Vh_{k}^{\prime}&amp;=\overline{A}Vh_{k-1}^{\prime}+\overline{B}x_{k}\\
y_{k}&amp;=\overline{C}Vh_{k}^{\prime}+\overline{D}x_{k}\end{aligned}\right.\,\Rightarrow\,\left\{\begin{aligned} h_{k}^{\prime}&amp;=V^{-1}\overline{A}Vh_{k-1}^{\prime}+V^{-1}\overline{B}x_{k}\\
y_{k}&amp;=\overline{C}Vh_{k}^{\prime}+\overline{D}x_{k}\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.113)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The new recurrence matrix <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{-1}\overline{A}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{-1}\overline{A}V</annotation></semantics></math> will be diagonal for some matrix <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> if we require <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{A}</annotation></semantics></math> to be diagonalizable. Fortunately, the set of diagonalizable matrices is dense, meaning that we can approximate any matrix with a diagonalizable one to arbitrary precision.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">The associative scan view</h5>

<div id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">So far, we have seen that the recurrent view is <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(S)</annotation></semantics></math> but can’t be parallelized, and that the convolutional view is <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(S\log S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(S\log S)</annotation></semantics></math> but can be parallelized. In this section, we will see another way of achieving parallelization leveraging the associative scan. We would like to remark that this is only applicable to training, for inference, the recurrent view is always used.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As motivation, consider the problem of computing the cumulative sum of an array <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>. This task is <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, and it does not seem easily parallelizable, because in order to compute <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{sum}(a[:n])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>sum</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sum}(a[:n])</annotation></semantics></math> one needs <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{sum}(a[:n-1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>sum</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sum}(a[:n-1])</annotation></semantics></math>. However, with enough processors one can bring down the runtime to <math id="Ch2.S3.SS3.SSSx4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log S)</annotation></semantics></math> (see Figure <a href="#Ch2.F5" title="Figure 2.5 ‣ The associative scan view ‣ 2.3.3 State Space Models and Linear RNNs ‣ 2.3 Sequence-to-sequence models ‣ Chapter 2 Theoretical background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a> for an overview of the algorithm). Interestingly, this can be done with any associative binary operator. In the rest of this section we will “lift” an affine recurrence into a parallel scan.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Associative scan)<span id="Thmdefinition14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given an array of elements <math id="Thmdefinition14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[e_{1},e_{2},...,e_{n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[e_{1},e_{2},...,e_{n}]</annotation></semantics></math> with an associative binary operation <math id="Thmdefinition14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> between them, an associative scan outputs the array <math id="Thmdefinition14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[e_{1},e_{1}\bullet e_{2},...,e_{1}\bullet\dots\bullet e_{n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[e_{1},e_{1}\bullet e_{2},...,e_{1}\bullet\dots\bullet e_{n}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
