<td id="Ch4.T2.3.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">7,272,704</td></tr>
<tr id="Ch4.T2.3.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch4.T2.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">1 pooling layer</th>
<td id="Ch4.T2.3.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">[2]</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.3.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">[12, 12]</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.3.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">7,268,608</td></tr>
<tr id="Ch4.T2.3.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch4.T2.3.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">No pooling</th>
<td id="Ch4.T2.3.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">[]</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.3.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">[36]</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.3.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">7,267,840</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="Ch4.T2.4" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<p id="Ch4.T2.4.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(b) Training performance and evaluation metrics</span></p>
<table id="Ch4.T2.4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training speed <math id="Ch4.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Test NLL <math id="Ch4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FID <math id="Ch4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">IS <math id="Ch4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Baseline</th>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11.45 epochs/h</span></td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.854</span> (1.854)</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.46</span></td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6.46</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Ch4.T2.4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch4.T2.4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">1 pooling layer</th>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">6.69 epochs/h</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.882 (1.853)</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">6.85</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">2.03</td></tr>
<tr id="Ch4.T2.4.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Ch4.T2.4.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">No pooling</th>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">6.11 epochs/h</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">1.865 <span id="Ch4.T2.4.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1.852)</span></td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">2.95</td>
<td id="Ch4.T2.4.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">3.33</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Ch4.T2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4.2</span>: </span><span id="Ch4.T2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Pooling importance<span id="Ch4.T2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (SC09). All models had 36 RG-LRU layers and were trained on a v3-128 TPU pod. Using pooling greatly accelerates training, improves perceptual metrics (FID and IS), and prevents overfitting. We report final negative log-likelihood (NLL) on the test set, with the best result (lowest validation loss) in parentheses. The samples used to compute the FID and IS scores were generated using the best model according to the validation loss.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Ch4.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02206v1/pooling-overfitting.svg" id="Ch4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/215;" width="286" height="215"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch4.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4.8</span>: </span><span id="Ch4.F8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Effect of pooling on overfitting<span id="Ch4.F8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (SC09). Pooling reduces overfitting, as shown by the test log-likelihood curve.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Ch4.S5.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Effect of <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="Ch4.S5.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch4.S5.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As explained in Section <a href="#Ch3.S2" title="3.2 Pooling ‣ Chapter 3 Poolformer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, the <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> parameter controls the expressivity of the weight matrices within the pooling layers. For example, if <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=1</annotation></semantics></math> there are no constraints on the weight matrices, and if <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=D</annotation></semantics></math> the weight matrices are diagonal. The higher the value of <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, the lower the expressivity and the number of parameters. In Table <a href="#Ch4.T3" title="Table 4.3 ‣ Effect of 𝐺 ‣ 4.5 Pooling Experiments ‣ Chapter 4 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> we see that setting <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=1</annotation></semantics></math> results in very unstable training.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="Ch4.T3.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
