</section>
<section id="Ch4.S5.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Depth-wise Analysis</h4>

<div id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A central motivation for using pooling is to enable better modeling of long-range dependencies. In our case, we investigate this behavior through the lens of the complex parameter <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, which governs how information is retained across timesteps in the RG-LRU.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The parameter <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{C}^{\frac{D}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{C}^{\frac{D}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\sigma(\Lambda)\cdot e^{i\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\sigma(\Lambda)\cdot e^{i\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{D}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{D}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{D}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{D}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> are learned parameters. The magnitude <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a|=\sigma(\Lambda)\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{D}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a|=\sigma(\Lambda)\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{D}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> determines how quickly the recurrent state decays over time: smaller values cause faster decay (short-term memory), while values close to 1 allow information to persist longer (long-term memory).</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use the average magnitude of <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> at each depth as a proxy for the temporal range that each layer is sensitive to. Specifically, values of <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a|\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a|\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math> indicate layers that are better equipped to model long-range dependencies, whereas layers with <math id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a|\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a|\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math> tend to focus on short-term patterns.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch4.S5.SSx3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In our experiments, it seems that deeper layers handle long-term dependencies, while shallower layers (especially the last ones) focus on short-term features. See Figure <a href="#Ch4.F9" title="Figure 4.9 ‣ Depth-wise Analysis ‣ 4.5 Pooling Experiments ‣ Chapter 4 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a> for more information.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch4.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02206v1/analysis-short-ring-baseline-bars.svg" id="Ch4.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/215;" width="286" height="215"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Ch4.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4.9</span>: </span><span id="Ch4.F9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Mean magnitude of <math id="Ch4.F9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> across model depth<span id="Ch4.F9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (baseline model, SC09). This plot shows how the average magnitude <math id="Ch4.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a|</annotation></semantics></math> evolves across the layers of the model. Deeper layers exhibit values closer to 1, indicating slower decay and a bias toward long-range dependencies. In contrast, shallower layers (especially at the end) show smaller magnitudes, suggesting they focus more on short-term features.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch4.S6" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4.6 </span>Scaling Study</h3>

<div id="Ch4.S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch4.S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recurrent neural networks are forced to compress the context into a fixed-size hidden state, which makes them efficient but limits their effectiveness. Thus, a larger hidden state should make the model more effective but slower <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch4.S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch4.S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this experiment, we adopt a pooling configuration of <math id="Ch4.S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2,4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2,4]</annotation></semantics></math>, a layer configuration of <math id="Ch4.S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[4,4,4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[4,4,4]</annotation></semantics></math>, and modify the dimension of the recurrence. In Figure <a href="#Ch4.F10" title="Figure 4.10 ‣ 4.6 Scaling Study ‣ Chapter 4 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a> and Table <a href="#Ch4.T4" title="Table 4.4 ‣ 4.6 Scaling Study ‣ Chapter 4 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> we see that increasing the recurrence dimension improves performance. Increasing the model dimension significantly raises the parameter count,
which leads to overfitting.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="Ch4.T4.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="Ch4.T4.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch4.T4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch4.T4.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model dim.</span></td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch4.T4.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recurrence dim.</span></td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch4.T4.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Num. params.</span></td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="Ch4.T4.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Test NLL <math id="Ch4.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="Ch4.T4.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Poolformer</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">128</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">256</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">4,054,528</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1.858 (1.853)</td></tr>
<tr id="Ch4.T4.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Poolformer</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">13,295,360</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.908 (1.866)</td></tr>
<tr id="Ch4.T4.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Poolformer</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">384</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">27,779,072</td>
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.917 (1.862)</td></tr>
<tr id="Ch4.T4.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Ch4.T4.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Poolformer</td>
